From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:52:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Obtain the storage bottle map in the backend

indexedDB.open() and deleteDatabase() asked the client storage thread
for the global's local storage bottle map and blocked the script
thread until it replied, and so did the teardown of a window or
worker. The bottle map is only needed by the backend, to create and
delete the database's files.

Script now sends what is needed to obtain it, the client storage
handle and the webview, as a StorageBottleSource with OpenDatabase and
DeleteDatabase, and the manager obtains the map when it handles the
request. A failure reaches script as the request's error event (an
OperationError, as the exception before) instead of an exception. On
teardown, AbortPendingUpgrades no longer carries a map: reverting an
aborted upgrade of a new database uses the map of its open request.

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 105 passed, 1 skipped, as before. Host SpiderMonkey WPT IndexedDB/ plus /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ (8 processes): 3,250 of 4,511 IndexedDB subtests pass (P1's tip: 3,251) and all /_mozilla/ ones; the difference is the one unexpected result, idbfactory-origin-isolation.html TIMEOUT, which also timed out in P0.1's and P0.2's baseline runs and passed 5 of 5 alone. `./mach test-tidy`: only the known libsqlite3-sys advisory.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote the change and ran the host tests and WPT)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
